    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1052">

                <pb facs="0920" n="908" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg908"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4061: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Haiti</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Sparks</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-10-04T01:00:00-05:00">October 4, 1940—1
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. With reference to my despatch No. 1029, September 28.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d1052-f1"/> The Fiscal Representative informed the Minister of
                    Finance that 200,000 gourdes could be added to the estimate of revenues if the
                    French commercial treaty<anchor n="40" xml:id="d1052-f2"/> were cancelled. The
                    budget as finally drafted <pb facs="0921" n="909" xml:id="pg909"/> does not
                    include this additional revenue. The Finance Minister declared to the Fiscal
                    Representative that the Minister of Foreign Affairs tenaciously opposed, pending
                    the outcome of his negotiations with the French Government which apparently are
                    only for the purpose of suspending the treaty.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sparks</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1052-f1" n="39" xml:id="d1052-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1052-f2" n="40" xml:id="d1052-f2-content">
                <p>Commercial Convention, with Protocol, between France and Haiti, signed at Paris,
                    June 24, 1938. For text, see <hi rendition="#italic">Le Moniteur</hi>, July 11,
                    1938, p. 451, and August 8, 1938, p. 515.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
